.Dd July 13, 2026
.Dt XTC_SAGA 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_saga_create ,
.Nm xtc_saga_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_saga_step ,
.Nm xtc_saga_run ,
.Nm xtc_saga_n_steps ,
.Nm xtc_saga_n_completed ,
.Nm xtc_saga_failed_step ,
.Nm xtc_saga_last_error ,
.Nm xtc_saga_compensate_failed
.Nd multi-step coordination with compensation (sagas)
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxtc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc_saga.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_create "xtc_saga_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_saga_destroy "xtc_saga_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_step "xtc_saga_t *s" "xtc_saga_fn action" "xtc_saga_fn compensate" "void *ctx"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_run "xtc_saga_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_n_steps "const xtc_saga_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_n_completed "const xtc_saga_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_failed_step "const xtc_saga_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_last_error "const xtc_saga_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_saga_compensate_failed "const xtc_saga_t *s"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Nm saga
is a sequence of
.Pq forward action , compensating action
pairs run in order, on the calling fiber, as ordinary
synchronous-looking C functions.  If a forward action fails, every
already-completed step's compensation runs in REVERSE order, undoing
the work the saga had done so far, and
.Fn xtc_saga_run
returns the ORIGINAL failing step's error code.  If every forward
action succeeds,
.Fn xtc_saga_run
returns
.Dv XTC_OK
and no compensation ever runs.
.Pp
This is the distributed-transaction
.Dq saga
pattern: no lock is held across steps and there is no two-phase-commit
coordinator, just a forward action and a hand-written undo per step.
It is the natural fit for a multi-step workflow where each step
already has an obvious inverse
.Pq e.g. Dq reserve inventory No / Dq release inventory ,
.Dq debit account No / Dq credit account back .
.Pp
Each step's action and compensate function has the signature
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef int (*xtc_saga_fn)(void *ctx);
.Ed
.Pp
and returns the usual
.Dv XTC_OK
/ negative
.Dv XTC_E_*
convention used everywhere else in this library.
.Fa ctx
is whatever the caller passed to
.Fn xtc_saga_step
(typically per-step state: a request payload, an id to undo, a handle
to release).  A step's
.Fa compensate
may be
.Dv NULL
for a step with no undo
.Pq e.g. a pure read ;
.Fn xtc_saga_run
then skips compensating it.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_saga_create
allocates an empty saga.
.Fn xtc_saga_step
appends one step; steps run in the order added.  Steps cannot be
added once
.Fn xtc_saga_run
has started.
.Fn xtc_saga_run
runs the saga
.Pq at most once; create a new one to run again .
.Fn xtc_saga_destroy
frees the saga handle; it does not touch step
.Fa ctx
pointers, which remain caller-owned.
.Pp
.Sy Unrecoverable saga :
if a compensation itself returns an error while the reverse walk is
undoing completed steps, that is a documented failure mode this
library does not silently swallow.
.Fn xtc_saga_run
logs it loudly
.Pq to stderr, naming the step and both error codes ,
continues running the REMAINING compensations in reverse order
regardless
.Pq one broken undo must not also skip cleanup further back ,
and the overall return value becomes
.Dv XTC_E_INTERNAL
instead of the original step's error code, so a caller can always tell
.Dq a step failed and every compensation ran cleanly
apart from
.Dq a step failed AND compensation itself is broken .
.Fn xtc_saga_compensate_failed
reports the latter case after a run;
.Fn xtc_saga_last_error
still reports the ORIGINAL forward failure's code for diagnostics even
when the overall return value was overridden to
.Dv XTC_E_INTERNAL .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_saga_n_steps ,
.Fn xtc_saga_n_completed ,
and
.Fn xtc_saga_failed_step
are introspection helpers, primarily for tests and logging: the total
step count, how many actions completed successfully on the last run,
and the
.Pq 0-based
index of the step whose action failed
.Pq -1 if none has failed .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_saga_create
and
.Fn xtc_saga_step
return
.Dv XTC_OK
or a negative
.Dv XTC_E_*
code
.Pq Dv XTC_E_INVAL No for a bad argument or a step added after
.Fn xtc_saga_run
started; Dv XTC_E_NOMEM No on allocation failure .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_saga_run
returns
.Dv XTC_OK
if every step succeeded;
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
if
.Fa s
is
.Dv NULL
or the saga was already run; the FAILING STEP'S error code if a step
failed and every triggered compensation succeeded; or
.Dv XTC_E_INTERNAL
if a step failed AND at least one compensation also failed
.Pq the unrecoverable-saga condition .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_saga_destroy
returns no value.  The remaining functions return the queried count /
index / code
.Pq 0 No or -1 No on a Dv NULL No saga, per field .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int reserve_inventory(void *ctx);
int release_inventory(void *ctx);
int charge_card(void *ctx);
int refund_card(void *ctx);
int ship_order(void *ctx);      /* no compensate: shipping cannot be undone */

xtc_saga_t *s;
int rc;

xtc_saga_create(&s);
xtc_saga_step(s, reserve_inventory, release_inventory, &order);
xtc_saga_step(s, charge_card,       refund_card,        &order);
xtc_saga_step(s, ship_order,        NULL,               &order);

rc = xtc_saga_run(s);
if (rc == XTC_E_INTERNAL) {
	/* A compensation itself failed; already logged.  Escalate --
	 * this order needs a human, xtc_saga_last_error(s) has the
	 * original failure and xtc_saga_failed_step(s) the step index. */
} else if (rc != XTC_OK) {
	/* A step failed but every compensation ran cleanly; nothing
	 * from this order is left in a partially-applied state. */
}
xtc_saga_destroy(s);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_async 3 ,
.Xr xtc_fsm 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_supervisor 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
Appeared in xtc 0.1, per PLAN.md section 19.5.
.Sh CAVEATS
A saga action runs synchronously on the calling fiber; it does not
itself provide concurrency or timeouts.  A step that needs to await
asynchronous work
.Pq an RPC, a spawned sub-task
does so internally using the existing primitives
.Pq Xr xtc_async 3 Ns 's Fn xtc_await , Xr xtc_proc 3 Ns 's Fn xtc_recv
and simply blocks the calling fiber until that work resolves before
returning -- a saga step is an ordinary function, not a new async
abstraction.
